==Russian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA}}
** {{IPA|ru|[mˠät̪]}}
* {{rhymes|ru|at|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{wp|ru:+ (шах+ы)}}

{{bor+|ru|fr|mat}}, short for {{m|fr|[[échec]] et mat}}, from {{der|ru|ar|شَاهُ مَاتَ}}, ultimately from {{der|ru|fa|شاه مات|tr=šâh mât|t=the king is amazed}}.

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+|adj=ма́товый}}

# {{lb|ru|chess}} [[checkmate]], [[mate]] (Russian notation: [[×]])

=====Declension=====
{{ru-noun-table}}

===Etymology 2===
{{bor+|ru|fr|mat}}, probably from {{der|ru|la|mattus}}.

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+|n=sg}}

# {{lb|ru|singular only}} [[mat]], [[matte]] [[finish]], [[frost]] ''(glass)''

=====Declension=====
{{ru-noun-table|n=sg}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ru|ма́товый}}

===Etymology 3===
{{wp|ru:+ (покрытие)}}
[[File:Turnmatte.jpg|thumb|{{lang|ru|гимнасти́ческий мат}}]]

{{bor+|ru|en|mat}} or {{bor|ru|nl|mat}}.

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+}}

# [[mat]], [[floor mat]] {{gloss|woven floor covering, or soft floor pad in athletics}}

=====Declension=====
{{ru-noun-table}}

===Etymology 4===
{{wp|ru:Русский +}}

Abbreviated from the expression {{m|ru|[[матерный|ма́терная]] [[брань]]}}, ultimately from {{m|ru|мать|gloss=mother}}.<ref>{{cite-book|ru|author=Н. М. Шанский|author2=Т. А. Боброва|title=Школьный этимологический словарь русского языка. Происхождение слов|year=2004|publisher=Дрофа|chapter=''мат (3)''}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{ru-noun+|n=sg}}

# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} [[foul language]]; language that includes obscene words deriving from a small set of roots for sex, sexual organs and sexuality
#: {{syn|ru|матерщи́на}}
#: {{uxi|ru|[[покрыва́ть]] '''ма́том'''|to heap [[scurrilous]] abuse on someone}}

=====Declension=====
{{ru-noun-table|n=sg}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ru|матери́ть|g=impf}}, {{l|ru|матери́ться|g=impf}}
* {{l|ru|матерщи́на|g=f}}
* {{l|ru|матерщи́нник|g=m-an}}
* {{l|ru|мать-перема́ть}}
* {{l|ru|матюка́ть|g=impf}}, {{l|ru|матюка́ться|g=impf}} ({{l|ru|матюга́ть|g=impf}}, {{l|ru|матюга́ться|g=impf}})
* {{l|ru|матю́к|g=m}} ({{l|ru|матю́г|g=m}})
* {{l|ru|матюга́льник|g=m}}

